 pub-id-type="pmid">22026428</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R8"><label>8</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Glazer</surname><given-names>RI</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>XY</given-names></name><name><surname>Yuan</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Yin</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Musashi1: a stem cell marker no longer in search of a function</article-title><source>Cell cycle</source><year>2008</year><volume>7</volume><issue>17</issue><fpage>2635</fpage><lpage>2639</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18719393</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R9"><label>9</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Glazer</surname><given-names>RI</given-names></name><name><surname>Vo</surname><given-names>DT</given-names></name><name><surname>Penalva</surname><given-names>LO</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Musashi1: an RBP with versatile functions in normal and cancer stem cells</article-title><source>Front Biosci</source><year>2012</year><volume>17</volume><fpage>54</fpage><lpage>64</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="R10"><label>10</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Okano</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Kawahara</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Toriya</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Nakao</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Shibata</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Imai</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Function of RNA-binding protein Musashi-1 in stem cells</article-title><source>Exp Cell Res</source><year>2005</year><volume>306</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>349</fpage><lpage>356</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15925591</pub-id></element-citation><